  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the individual to consider the proportion of probability assigned to favorable outcomes and to prefer the lottery with a greater portion of probability on favorable outcomes (defined as left-skewed). In this case, Lottery A has 25% favorable probability, Lottery B has 20%, so A is more left-skewed according to the reason's definition. Therefore, the reason would prefer A. However, the individual chose B. Moreover, in the verbal report, the individual does not mention skewness, distribution, or favorable probability mass at all. The reasoning is based solely on the size of the prize and a comparison of probabilities without reference to asymmetry or distribution shape. Thus, the individual did not consider the skewness-based rule. Even though the information is available, it was not used in the justification. The individual's reasoning is based on expected value or prize magnitude, not on skewness. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
